  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>80</x>
      <y>30</y>
      <w>7480</w>
      <h>240</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>PhotoPilot | Section 3 - UML Class Diagram
Read left to right by package. F01-F11 tags identify responsibilities; {text} records constraints and pattern roles.
Standard Java types: UUID, Optional, List, Set, Map, Path, URI, HttpClient, Instant, Duration, LocalDate and ZonedDateTime.
Methods use name(parameter: Type): ReturnType; void returns omitted. Interfaces and abstract names/operations are italic.
Native UML relationships: dashed open arrow = dependency; dashed hollow triangle = realization; solid hollow triangle = generalization.
Solid line = association; hollow diamond = shared aggregation; filled diamond = exclusive composition (diamond at owner).
Reference boxes repeat an existing classifier solely to keep cross-package wiring readable; they are not additional Java types.
Sources: current Stage1.docx Sections 1-2; stage1.pdf Task 2.1; Project-Instruction.pdf; EECS3311-03-UML pp.15-26 and UML-II.
fontsize=16
bg=#FFFDEB</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes />
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>80</x>
      <y>9250</y>
      <w>3640</w>
      <h>200</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Runtime boundaries
--
LLM failure returns Result errors, never fabricated recommendations.
Inventory, session persistence, calculations and EXIF statistics bypass the agent.
PhotoPilotAgent runs a bounded model/tool/evidence loop; output schema validation
precedes domain validation. Tool access is an allowlist, with consent checked locally.
Agent tools are read-only: no autonomous saves, inventory changes or plan approval.
fontsize=15
bg=#FFFDEB</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes />
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>3920</x>
      <y>9250</y>
      <w>3640</w>
      <h>200</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Planning invariants
--
F03 retains original text, clarification questions and user confirmation.
F06 contains capabilities only. F07 rejects incompatible candidates and excludes
unverified combinations from usable recommendations; ranking preserves candidate IDs.
GearMatchingTool obtains deterministic candidates only; it does not invoke rank().
F10 uses approved input, controlled commands, validation, then user approval and save.
fontsize=15
bg=#FFFDEB</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes />
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>80</x>
      <y>9470</y>
      <w>3640</w>
      <h>200</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Ownership and assumptions
--
Saved session plans/reviews are owned records; copied GearSnapshot values preserve
history after inventory removal. Warn using referencingGear() before removal.
Loadout values copied into a plan are exclusively owned by that revision.
JSON persistence and Draft -&gt; Planned -&gt; Completed -&gt; Reviewed are design choices.
External provider/library brands and the optional device-location adapter remain undecided.
fontsize=15
bg=#FFFDEB</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes />
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>3920</x>
      <y>9470</y>
      <w>3640</w>
      <h>200</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Source and scope checks
--
The current F03 AI paragraph correctly describes natural-language parsing.
The previously reported location/distance/permission wording is absent from this version.
Order-image bytes enter AI only as user-approved SanitizedImage; discard after use.
JPEG/EXIF summaries use extracted values and mark incomplete evidence.
No aesthetic scores, image editing, client management or social publishing are introduced.
fontsize=15
bg=#FFFDEB</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes />
  </element>
